# HOWLBOX resource budget (read by scripts/verify_program.sh)
# Paper LC ~4,920 (spec §4); serial howler-class pipeline, H3 does not apply.
# The ONLY memory is the 256x30 H-phase remap delay line = 2 EBR.
WARN_LC=5500     # comfortable target (aim here)
MAX_LC=7200      # hard gate (~94% of die)
MAX_EBR=2        # exactly the remap delay line; anything else is a defect
MIN_FMAX=76      # full-clock (÷1) HD bar -- see the ÷2 note below.

# HD runs at ÷2 (TOML hd_clock_divisor=2): the program clock is prog_clk = 37.125 MHz.
# verify_program.sh currently (a) does NOT read hd_clock_divisor -> builds HD at ÷1,
# and (b) gates Fmax>=76 against 74.25 -- BOTH wrong for this program. Correct Gate-3
# HD assessment: build with HD_CLOCK_DIVISOR=2 and --freq 37.125, then require the
# 'u_core_top.prog_clk' domain to MEET 37.125 (measured ~70 MHz, ~1.9x margin) while
# the pixel/IO domain meets 74.25 (measured ~106 MHz). Until the script is
# divisor-aware, assess HD manually -- evidence in plans/howlbox/evidence/div2-*.log.
# NOTE: hd_dual + ÷2 does NOT build -- SDK core_top bug (dual+decimated-clock driver
# conflict), program-independent (stock howler fails identically); hd_dual+÷1 is fine.
